{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511153-are-mokery-breeds-expecially-yeren-compatible-with-other-splats","id":1511153,"title":"Are Mokery Breeds ( expecially Yeren ) compatible with other splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-09T13:43:32-07:00","id":1511153,"title":"Are Mokery Breeds ( expecially Yeren ) compatible with other splats?","content":"I've found nothing in the official books, so I guess we are in the realm of the homebrew.<br /> However, by logic, Rules as Intended:<br /> <br /> 1- could a Mockery Breed become a Fomor ( for example following Dr. Veridian program and becoming a Throwback, or watching the bane-tainted snuff films and becoming a Gorehound )?<br /> <br /> 2- could a MB be Embraced and become a... Mockery Abomination? A MB vampire, in short.<br /> <br /> 3- could a MB be spiritually twisted / empowered by a demon and become a demonic Thraal ( Dark Ages: Devil's Due )?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T14:02:51-07:00","id":1511154,"title":"","content":"Probably, the ones that have homid breeds most likely, and a soft maybe, respectively. There's probably more impetus for hypothetical mockery abominations to turn to becoming a Wyrm-puppet to preserve their Gnosis, and they probably don't suffer quite as much as the Garou and Fera. That said, I could also see some of them having serious downsides like the Rokea (permanent frenzy after embrace), and some might even explode like Kitsune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T22:22:07-07:00","id":1511328,"title":"","content":"1-There are a few werewolf formor, but they're extremely rare and specialized and most spirits can't possess garou, so it's probably the same with yeren. WoD tends to work under the idea that if you can think of it, there's magic for it, so there should at least be one spirit capable of doing it. <br /> <br /> 2- If it isn't killed by Gnosis and has a human form, yes. <br /> <br /> 3-If it has the awareness to get involved with a demon or spiritual inverter, then yes. These things need consent, so something like a war wolf wouldn't work. However, I'd caution about using devil's due mechanics. They work fine in a vacuum but not so well in other contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:53:48-07:00","id":1511387,"title":"","content":"The Yeren being already wyrm-tainted and having nothing to do with Gaia should make things easier for them in being embraced, I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T11:31:31-07:00","id":1511391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511153-are-mokery-breeds-expecially-yeren-compatible-with-other-splats?p=1511387#post1511387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yeren being already wyrm-tainted and having nothing to do with Gaia should make things easier for them in being embraced, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs don't like abominations either, so not necessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:08:52-07:00","id":1511514,"title":"","content":"On a differant approach I was tempted to have the mockery breeds as legitimate breeds. Specifically the samsa and yeren to represent gaia changing tact. The samsa representing a failsafe if all other options fail and gaia (or the wyrm) intiates a mass extinction event and the yeren representing gaias attempt to assert control in economic realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-13-2023, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T01:58:53-07:00","id":1524131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511153-are-mokery-breeds-expecially-yeren-compatible-with-other-splats?p=1511514#post1511514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a differant approach I was tempted to have the mockery breeds as legitimate breeds. Specifically the samsa and yeren to represent gaia changing tact. The samsa representing a failsafe if all other options fail and gaia (or the wyrm) intiates a mass extinction event and the yeren representing gaias attempt to assert control in economic realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>*points at the Apocalyptic Record* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T09:52:04-07:00","id":1524142,"title":"","content":"If anyting, Trunko - a killer whale killer Cryptid possessing polar bear's snowy-white fur, an elephantine trunk, and lobster-like tail - &quot;proves&quot; anything could happen<br /> The Loveland Frogs are Anurana whithout a question...<br /> As for the question, yes, the mokery breeds are just like every other breeds (just with very strong wyrmish tone) are compatible with other splats<br /> Especially considering there are always exceptions of the rule<br /> Take Sobek for example, Sutekh's 4th generation Mokol\u00e9 Abomination Child from the Isis Fragments (Embraced through rituals designed by the Dark God himself) who shouldn't even exist - Mokol\u00e9 In general are immune to the Embrace, resulting only in a Frenzied rampage that claims the life of the would-be sire and their own swift death once the sun rises - yet the God of Storms dark power owerwrote that &quot;rule&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-16-2023, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}